{"id": "EUVD-2026-97066", "enisaUuid": "bec1400a-e4c0-3138-b1b9-49c23f8c87fa", "description": "pH7Builder (pH7 Social Dating CMS) before 19.3.0 contains a CAPTCHA bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to skip form validation by supplying a client-chosen form ID to PFBC Form::isValid(). Attackers can load a CAPTCHA-free form like login or search, then submit its ID with contact, comment, forum, invite or signup data to automate abuse.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:58:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:54:04", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/commit/4758d7d2ebfd5772faa25ef728c14f8f452e82f4", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/blob/v19.2.0/_protected/app/system/modules/contact/forms/ContactForm.php#L33-L38", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ph7builder-before-19.3.0-captcha-bypass-via-client-chosen-form-id"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q5mq-9wc6-h8x8", "CVE-2026-108903"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c337094c-d5e1-3b3f-ab27-b0f02c695898", "product": {"name": "ph7builder", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}, "product_version": "0 <19.3.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7dd60b38-ac66-3122-9428-f290d1638833", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}], "isExploited": false}